Assembler Version 14
====================
Assembled by: version 13 (both instgen and asm)

Features Supported by This Assembler
-------------------------------------
All features from version 13, plus local labels and debug output:

Syntax:
- Non-standard (custom) mnemonic syntax: LDA#, LDAZ, STAZ, etc.
- DATA pseudo-instruction for raw byte emission
- Hex constants: $xx (1 byte) or $xxxx (2 bytes)
- Quoted strings with \n and \\ escapes
- Label definitions with PC value or explicit assignment (including label refs)
- PC setting via: * = $xxxx (with zero-fill on pass 2)
- Low byte (<) and high byte (>) operators on labels
- Relative branch labels (auto-detected via instruction flags)
- Labels as 2-byte operands
- Comments with semicolons
- Two-pass assembly
- .include directive
- .zeropage and .code section directives
- Command-line arguments: <assembler> <input> <output> [debug]
- Local labels with . prefix (new): .label scoped to enclosing global label

Directives:
- .include filename
- .zeropage - switches to zero page section
- .code - switches back to code section

Instruction set: same as version 13, plus:
- CMP,X (compare absolute indexed X - opcode $DD)

Error handling: same as version 13 (errors 1-D), plus:
- No file open (error E): attempt to read with no file open
- No global label for local (error F): local label used before any global label
- Invalid debug argument (error 10): third argument is not "debug"

New in this version (relative to version 13):
- Local labels (.label syntax): labels starting with . are scoped to the
  most recent global label. The assembler expands ".foo" to "globalname.foo"
  internally before storing in the hash table.
- CURR_GLOBAL buffer at $1C00: stores the name of the current global label
  for local label expansion
- update_global_label function: called when a non-assignment global label is
  defined, copies label name to CURR_GLOBAL buffer
- expand_local_label function: prepends CURR_GLOBAL to local label name
- Optional debug command-line argument: "debug" as third arg enables debug
  output (DEBUG_FLAG)
- New instruction: CMP,X (absolute indexed X)
- Hash table changed from split low/high ($80 offset) to 2-byte pointer
  entries (HASH is ASL'd to index pairs of bytes), using 256-byte table
  with 128 entries
- store_hash_value extracted to common.asm: separates value storage from
  token storage in hash_add, allowing caller to store value after hash_add
- LHASHTAB moved to $1E00, TOKEN moved to $1D00
- Error for reading with no file open (previously would silently fail)

Features Used in This Assembler's Source Code
----------------------------------------------
- Non-standard mnemonic syntax (LDA#, LDAZ, STAZ, BITZ, INCZ, etc.)
- DATA pseudo-instruction
- DATA $00 for zero page variable allocation in .zeropage section
- Hex constants ($xx and $xxxx)
- Quoted strings with escape sequences
- Labels and label assignments (label = value)
- PC setting (* = $2000 and * = $FFFC for vectors)
- Low byte (<) and high byte (>) operators
- Labels as absolute 2-byte operands
- Comments (;)
- BRK with inline error code and message
- .include directive (out/inst.asm.out, environment.asm, common.asm,
  file_stack.asm, to_decimal.asm)
- .zeropage and .code section directives
- Command-line arg access: argc, argv
- File I/O: open, close, read, openout, write

New syntax used in source (relative to version 13):
- None (source does NOT use local labels; all labels are global)

Other source changes:
- CURR_GLOBAL buffer at $1C00 for tracking current global label name
- DEBUG_FLAG variable in zero page
- expand_local_label and update_global_label functions
- Hash table uses ASL HASH for 2-byte pointer entries (changed from
  HASH+$80 offset in v13)
- HTTPL/HTTPH temporary pointer added to hash_table.asm (replaces PL/PH
  from common.asm for hash table traversal)
- store_hash_value in common.asm stores value separately from store_token
